          "convergenceTargetId": "1767681762516",
          "id": "1767591589512",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767591589513_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given an array of results from a Kanban supplier performance analysis. - {{$context.$nodes.PREPARETOP5SUPPLIERS.$output.result}}\nEach element may either be an empty object {} or an object indicating that a supplier took longer than the expected replenishment lead time.\n\nYour task is to:\nTitle is Kanban Supplier Lead Time Deviation\n1. Ignore all empty objects.\n2. Consider only records where \"SLA_Breached\" is true\n3. Group the records by supplier using:\n   - SupplierName\n   - SupplierSiteName (if available)\n4. For each supplier (and site), calculate:\n   - Number of Kanban cards where the lead time was exceeded\n   - Average percentage by which the supplier exceeded the expected lead time\n   - Maximum percentage exceedance observed\n5. Inform the user in a single sentence in minimal words that Default view shows suppliers with lead times exceeding expected values by over 2%\n\n6. **Chart Widget**\n Generate a chartWidget of type 'Bar'\n   - X-axis: Supplier name (include site name in brackets if available)\n   - Y-axis: Average lead time exceedance percentage. Specify that this is the Average Deviation% as key on y axis\n\nIMPORTANT DISPLAY RULES:\n- Do NOT display or mention any technical IDs (SupplierId, SupplierSiteId, KanbanCardId, PullSequenceId, etc.).\n- Use only human-readable names.\n- If SupplierSiteName is missing, refer to it as \"Primary Site\".\n- Do NOT use the term \"SLA\" anywhere in the output.\n\nInterpretation rules:\n- \"BreachPercent\" represents how much the actual supplier processing time exceeded the expected lead time.\n- Percentages should be rounded to 1 decimal place.\n\nOutput format:\n- Then list suppliers in descending order of average lead time exceedance.\n\nIf no supplier exceeded the expected lead time, respond with:\n\"No lead time breaches were detected for the analyzed Kanban cards.\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Final Answer for query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FINAL_ANSWER_FOR_QUERY",
          "id": "1767681795167",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767681795168_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are given an array of results from a Kanban supplier lead time analysis:\n {{$context.$nodes.PREPARETOP5SUPPLIERS.$output.result}} and user query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nEach element in the array is either:\n- an empty object {}, or\n- an object indicating that a supplier exceeded the expected replenishment lead time for a specific item.\n\nYour task is to produce a MULTI-RECORD TABLE WIDGET suitable for Oracle Fusion UI.\n\n---\nFirst:\n1. check if the query is out of context. If it is return a message saying this is out of scope.\n\nElse:\nPROCESSING RULES:\n\n1. Ignore all empty objects.\n2. Consider only records where \"SLA_Breached\" is true.\n3. Treat each remaining record as a separate row (no aggregation).\n4. Extract the following fields for each row:\n   - SupplierName\n   - ItemNumber (or ItemName if available)\n   - BreachPercent\n\n---\n\nDISPLAY RULES (MANDATORY):\n\n- Do NOT display or mention any technical IDs.\n- Do NOT use the term \"SLA\" anywhere.\n- Use only human-readable values.\n- Round BreachPercent to **1 decimal place**.\n- If item information is missing, display \"Not specified\".\nIf filtered records count = 0, output exactly: \"No lead time devaitions found for this <item>.\"\nDo not output table/widget/headers when empty.\n\n---\n\nTABLE SCHEMA (STRICT – ORACLE MULTI-RECORD WIDGET):\n\nReturn an object with the following structure:\n\n{\n  \"type\": \"multiRecord\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"supplier\",\n      \"label\": \"Supplier\",\n      \"type\": \"text\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"item\",\n      \"label\": \"Item\",\n      \"type\": \"text\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"key\": \"breachPercent\",\n      \"label\": \"Lead Time Exceeded (%)\",\n      \"type\": \"text\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rows\": []\n}\n\n---\n\nROW MAPPING LOGIC:\n\nFor each qualifying record, add a row in this format:\n\n{\n  \"supplier\": \"<Supplier Name>\",\n  \"item\": \"<Item Number or Item Name>\",\n  \"breachPercent\": <numeric percentage>,\n  \"rowStyle\": \"<severity>\"\n}\n\n---\n\nCONDITIONAL HIGHLIGHTING RULES:\n\nSet \"rowStyle\" based on breachPercent:\n\n- breachPercent > 100 → \"error\"        (red)\n- breachPercent between 50 and 100 → \"warning\" (amber)\n- breachPercent < 50 → \"normal\"\n\nThese styles will be used by the UI for visual emphasis.\n\n---\n\nSORTING RULE:\n\n- Sort rows by \"breachPercent\" in descending order.\n\n---\n\nEMPTY RESULT HANDLING:\n\nIf no records exceed the expected lead time, return a proper message that should answer the user's query.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Fill Parameters"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
